Opus 5.5, 2026-11-22.  MEASURED: after IO::File->new the variable's value is a p-typeglob (*Symbol::GEN0), whose IO slot the handle table holds.  p-flush-dropped-handle's inline gate (%p-may-hold-handle-p) admits a glob and an fdopen alias; %p-flush-dropped-value / %p-flush-dropped-handle-1 take the glob's stream from the handle table (%p-resolve-fh: lookups only; a tied handle's placeholder is no descriptor stream, so no method runs) and peel an fdopen alias (%p-stream-target: IO::Handle->new_from_fd).  Probes scratch/s543g/probes (the s543g worktree)/m6: IO::File (both statements), new_from_fd, gensym, a blessed glob with "" overloading, a handle returned from a sub = perl (base 0); a tied handle: no FETCH / CLOSE (= perl); read / pipe / socket / in-memory: = perl; `\*FH` of a named glob the program still uses: its bytes arrive early (perl 0, PCL 5: harmless, documented); File::Temp's unlink is its DESTROY (exit-only by the USER's ruling); STDOUT / STDERR interleaving base = tree (fd <= 2 is never flushed).  Guard Pl/t/fh-collect-01.t row 9.
